    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d326">

                <pb facs="0455" n="443" sameAs="frus:frus1946v07/pg443"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.24591/5–146: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Chargé in Iran</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Ward</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">us urgent   most immediate</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1946-05-01T18:00:00-04:00">May 1, 1946—6
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>383. Please ascertain Iranian Govt’s plans for compliance by May 6 with request
                    embodied in Security Council resolution of Apr 4 “to report to the Council
                    whether the withdrawal of all Soviet troops from the whole of Iran has been
                    completed.” If plans are negative or uncertain, you should make clear to Qavam
                    that US Govt considers that compliance by members of the United Nations with
                    requests of Council is of paramount importance in strengthening effectiveness of
                    that organization. Reply urgently.</p>
                <p>Sent to Tehran, repeated to N.Y.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
